flowchart TB
    accTitle: One result — different uses on screen and in follow-ups
    accDescr: A successful response supplies the screen with all loaded rows, while future AI questions receive recent context with all loaded rows per retained turn. The history budget removes whole turns, without sampling rows. Browser table actions and CSV use the loaded snapshot. A separate CSV API reruns SQL and may observe newer data. New chat or reload clears local conversation state.
    %% Companion guides: docs/frontend.md, docs/database.md, docs/query-agent.md

    RESULT["Successful response"]:::work
    SCREEN["On screen: Keep all loaded rows"]:::view
    TABLE["Sort, page, and resize: Use only the loaded rows"]:::view
    CSV["Download CSV: Same rows, original database order"]:::data
    HISTORY["For follow-up questions: All loaded rows per retained turn"]:::work
    BUDGET["History budget: Drop whole turns above 40 messages or 120,000 characters"]:::note
    NEXT["Next question: Start a fresh request"]:::view
    RESET["New chat or reload: Clears local conversation state"]:::note
    API["Separate CSV API: Reruns SQL and may see newer data"]:::note

    RESULT --> SCREEN --> TABLE --> CSV
    RESULT --> HISTORY --> NEXT
    SCREEN -.-> RESET
    HISTORY -.-> RESET
    BUDGET -.-> HISTORY
    CSV -.->|Different download option| API

    classDef view fill:#eff6ff,stroke:#2563eb,color:#172033,stroke-width:1.5px;
    classDef work fill:#f5f3ff,stroke:#7c3aed,color:#4c1d95,stroke-width:1.5px;
    classDef data fill:#ecfdf5,stroke:#059669,color:#064e3b,stroke-width:1.5px;
    classDef note fill:#fffbeb,stroke:#d97706,color:#78350f,stroke-width:1.5px;
